# Feature Workflow

## Delegate, then integrate

When a feature has two or more independent pieces, the lead agent splits it, launches one
subagent per piece, and integrates the results itself.

The lead owns:

- The split, and the contracts between pieces: types, function signatures, endpoints.
  Contracts are decided before any subagent starts, never negotiated between them.
- Integration, running the app, and the final review.
- Keeping the docs index current.

Every subagent prompt states:

- The goal, and the exact files that subagent owns. It must not edit anything outside them.
- The contract it implements, written out verbatim rather than described.
- Which docs to read first.
- How to verify its own work, and what done looks like.

## When not to delegate

Single-file changes, bug fixes, and anything under roughly thirty minutes. Briefing an
agent costs more than doing the work.

## Integration is not optional

Subagent output is a proposal until the lead has run the whole thing and seen it work.
Never merge parallel work and declare it done without executing it.
